{"slug":"potamogeton-crispus","plant":{"taxon":"Potamogeton crispus","family":"Potamogetonaceae","rank":"species","gbif_key":5301162,"wikidata":"Q157863","iucn":"LC","gbif_occurrences":122706,"common_name":"Curled pondweed","names":[{"source":"culpeper","name":"Water-Caltrops","monograph_id":"cul:061-water-caltrops","confidence":"low","note":"Names belong to Trapa natans, said absent; the two described English kinds are pondweeds (Potamogeton)."}],"n_compounds":0,"top_compounds":[],"epmc_total":221,"trials":0,"claims":[{"concept_id":"envenomation","dsc":0,"cul":1,"persistent":false,"epmc_pair":0,"lift":0.87,"evidence_tier":"unstudied"},{"concept_id":"inflammation","dsc":0,"cul":1,"persistent":false,"epmc_pair":0,"lift":0.08,"evidence_tier":"unstudied"},{"concept_id":"mouth_gums","dsc":0,"cul":1,"persistent":false,"epmc_pair":0,"lift":0.52,"evidence_tier":"unstudied"},{"concept_id":"poisoning","dsc":0,"cul":1,"persistent":false,"epmc_pair":0,"lift":0.37,"evidence_tier":"unstudied"},{"concept_id":"scrofula","dsc":0,"cul":1,"persistent":false,"epmc_pair":0,"lift":0.72,"evidence_tier":"unstudied"},{"concept_id":"skin_ulcers","dsc":0,"cul":1,"persistent":false,"epmc_pair":0,"lift":0.75,"evidence_tier":"unstudied"},{"concept_id":"sore_throat","dsc":0,"cul":1,"persistent":false,"epmc_pair":0,"lift":0.78,"evidence_tier":"unstudied"},{"concept_id":"urolithiasis","dsc":0,"cul":1,"persistent":false,"epmc_pair":0,"lift":0.75,"evidence_tier":"unstudied"}],"lead_score":null},"texts":{"cul:061-water-caltrops":{"ref":"Culpeper, Complete Herbal: Water-Caltrops","headword":"Water-Caltrops","lang":"en","source":"culpeper","text":"They are under the dominion of the Moon, and being made into a poultice, are excellently good for hot inflammations, swellings, cankers, sore mouths and throats, being washed with the decoction; it cleanses and strengthens the neck and throat, and helps those swellings which, when people have, they say the almonds of the ears are fallen down. It is excellentl